-- 1535_repoint_dead_url_tail.sql
--
-- The verifiable part of the dead-URL long tail: 136 row-citations moved to the page OnTheIssues
-- actually has, and 98 moved to a Wayback capture that was checked to carry what the row asserts.
-- Nothing is retired, no stance value changes.
--   Review: data/stance-retirement/2026-08-02-dead-url-tail.md
--   Rollback: data/stance-retirement/2026-08-02-tail-rollback.json
--
-- 🔴 THIS TAIL IS MOSTLY NOT LINK ROT. Of 623 cited URLs the 08-02 sweep called GONE, 559 are still
-- dead on re-probe -- and Wayback has NEVER captured 518 of them (1,324 row-citations). That is not a
-- coverage gap. Wayback holds 3,000+ distinct URLs in the SAME directory as the ones we cite on
-- www.wbur.org/news/, www.mass.gov/info-details/, www.newtonma.gov/government/,
-- www.somervillema.gov/departments/ and www.ontheissues.org/House/, and not one capture of ours.
-- A URL that a heavily-crawled host never served and the archive never saw was, on the balance of
-- evidence, composed rather than visited. Those rows are NOT touched here: re-pointing cannot fix a
-- citation to a page that never existed, and whether they are re-researched or retired is not a call
-- this migration should make.
--
-- 🔴 GROUP L IS A GENUINE FIX, AND IT IS WHY THE WHOLE TAIL IS NOT WRITTEN OFF. OnTheIssues files a
-- politician under FOUR different shapes with no rule that predicts which -- /MA/Jim_McGovern.htm,
-- /House/Jahana_Hayes.htm, /Senate/Ed_Markey.htm and bare /Maura_Healey.htm -- and under the familiar
-- name, so Stephen Lynch is Steve_Lynch. Candidates came from the site's own /house.htm index (735
-- links), not from a guessed transform, and every one was fetched and confirmed.
--
-- ⚠ IDENTITY WAS CHECKED BY NAME **AND** CORROBORATION, NEVER BY NAME ALONE. OnTheIssues has pages for
-- several Robert Garcias, Mike Rogerses and John Rogerses. Where our own record had no state to check
-- against -- four 2026 candidates with no office row -- the page was confirmed against a specific in
-- the row's own reasoning: Robert Garcia's page carries "District 42", Andy Barr's carries Kentucky and
-- the Sugar Reform Act, Mike Rogers's carries Michigan, Pete Aguilar's California.
--
-- ⚠ GROUP A IS ROW-SCOPED, NOT URL-SCOPED. On four of these captures some rows check out and some do
-- not -- the Salt Lake County council release names three of the thirteen officials whose rows cite it
-- -- so only the rows the capture actually supports are moved. The other 15 stay on the dead URL and are
-- listed in the review. This is the Jemison rule from 1531 applied per row instead of per page.
--
-- ⚠ ONE CITED URL IS ON A HOST THAT NO LONGER RESOLVES THE PATH SHAPE AT ALL: Ghazala Hashmi has no
-- OnTheIssues page under any of the four shapes, so her 22 rows are held rather than pointed at
-- somebody else's page.

